WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.142 --> 00:00:03.002
-Our first guest tonight
is one of my favorites.

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:05.137
You'll be able to see him soon
in the movie "North Hollywood."

00:00:05.137 --> 00:00:08.274
Please welcome Vince Vaughn,
ladies and gentlemen!

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.609
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.244
That's -- That's what I'm --

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.113
That's what
I'm talking about, here.

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.146
Vince!

00:00:14.146 --> 00:00:15.581
-Good to see you, man.
-It is always --

00:00:15.581 --> 00:00:17.416
-Congrats on being
back in the studio.

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:19.385
-Oh, thank you, buddy.
Yeah, we got an audience.

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:20.786
It's unbelievable.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:22.255
-It's amazing.

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:24.891
Like seeing a terrific dolphin
released back into the ocean.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.092
It's nice to see.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.293
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.662
-That's exactly
how I'd describe it, yeah.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:32.632
You were with us
when we did our shows at home

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.734
and then in the other studio

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.337
and now back in our original
"Tonight Show" with an audience,

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.372
so I appreciate you
being a friend of the show.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:40.874
Thank you for
helping us out, buddy.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.341
-Yeah, great to be with you.

00:00:42.341 --> 00:00:44.243
Are you glad to be back?

00:00:44.243 --> 00:00:45.544
-It's amazing.

00:00:45.544 --> 00:00:48.814
I mean, to be honest,
the first show we came back,

00:00:48.814 --> 00:00:51.217
I was a little bit too emotional
just coming out,

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.752
'cause I was like --
I wasn't ready for it.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.254
I'm like, "Whew,
I need to tell jokes."

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:57.490
[ Laughs ]
But now it's the greatest.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.360
It feels like we're slowly
getting back to normal,

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.761
you know, so it feels good.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.796
-Yeah, for sure. And it's nice
to have a feeling about it

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.531
that you like, and I think
that's a good thing.

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:07.399
-Yeah. Yeah, thanks. Yeah.

00:01:07.399 --> 00:01:09.802
I was going to ask you, did you
watch the Derby this weekend?

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:10.936
Kentucky Derby?

00:01:10.936 --> 00:01:13.006
-You know, I usually always
watch the Derby.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.474
I never miss it.

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:17.343
But this year because of kids'
sports, I did miss the Derby.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:20.079
But I saw that Bob Baffert,
who's a great trainer,

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:22.115
that he had kind of a long shot
that won.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:24.217
-Yeah, it was unbelievable.

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.252
Yeah, I know -- What, do you
have to take the kids --

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.420
Are they playing baseball
or something?

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.824
-Yeah. There was a baseball game
and a soccer game,

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.059
and there was
traveling involved.

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:34.193
We've talked about this.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:36.029
For some reason,
you have to drive 35 minutes

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:38.731
to play other 9-year-olds.
It's a confusing process.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.702
I don't understand.
I don't understand it,

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:45.738
but I'm on the train.
It's not stopping,

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:48.541
but I don't understand.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:51.243
-And of course, they're playing
probably two different fields

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:52.879
and different times
and all that stuff?

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:53.913
-And then you can't find --

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.381
I don't know
which field is what.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:58.017
There's a field behind the field
and you didn't know about that.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.052
And people are in tears,
and you're late, and it's --

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:02.255
You know what I mean?
It's all complicated.

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.423
But I'm glad we're playing.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.024
I'm grateful the kids
are back playing sports.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.626
So, no complaints.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:08.994
Now, did you enjoy the Derby?
Was that an exciting --

00:02:08.994 --> 00:02:10.997
What happened that made this
memorable for you?

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.199
-I enjoyed it. I love -- I do --

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:16.068
For me, watching horse racing,
it reminds me of my childhood,

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:21.007
'cause that was like a treat
for us to go to like a smoky OTB

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:24.410
with a bunch of alcoholics,

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.780
and you just let the kids
run free, and, yeah.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:31.784
And Grandpa took me there, just
bet on horses and just gambled,

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:34.987
bunch of people gambling,
smoking cigarettes, and, yeah.

00:02:34.987 --> 00:02:36.322
-I had the same childhood.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.024
It was Arlington Park
in Chicago.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.727
And my dad would always take me,
and there were a group of kids

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:44.163
that would play tag
near the finish line.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:47.634
My dad would let me pick horses.
So there would be --

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.602
He would give me $2 a race.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.905
And whatever we won,
we would split, if I won.

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:53.072
And if I lost, we were even,

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.074
so I couldn't complain
about the setup.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.909
But, you know, you just
pick the horses by name,

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:58.511
and every now and then,
you'd hit a long shot.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:59.979
It felt like a nice day.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:02.648
-I don't know if I ever told you
about my worst investment ever.

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:05.050
Did I ever tell you about this?
-[ Laughs ] No. Please.

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:08.120
-So, this is
not that far long ago.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.589
But anyways, I was
on "Saturday Night Live,"

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:12.992
and this was the first time I
was actually making real money.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.061
And some guy
in my building said,

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.897
"Hey, Jimmy, do you want to
invest in a race horse?"

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.733
And I go, "Yes. Of course."

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.701
And so he's like, "Alright,
I'll get you details later."

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.804
And I go, "Oh, my God."
I called my dad and my mom.

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:26.972
I go, "I'm going to invest
in a race horse!

00:03:26.972 --> 00:03:29.208
I'm going to own a horse."

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:31.644
It's going to be fantastic.

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.012
And it was
a lot of money for me.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:35.014
And I called
my business manager.

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:37.383
He said, "Do not do this.
This is a disaster.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.218
This a waste of money.
Don't even do this."

00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:43.456
I go, "No, I got to do it.
I was raised -- I have to."

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:46.191
So I go, I'm going to go
to the stables every day.

00:03:46.191 --> 00:03:49.395
I'm going to comb it.
I'm going to brush its teeth.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:53.065
I don't care. I'm going to say,
"You are Sea Warrior,

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:55.401
and you're going to win
the Kentucky Derby."

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.403
And so, I called my friend
after I made the investment.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.105
And he goes --
I go, "When do you name it?

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:00.973
He goes, "What do you mean?
It's already named.

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:02.241
You don't name the horse.

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:04.176
It's named by like the sire
of the," you know --

00:04:04.176 --> 00:04:06.546
I go, "Oh, what's the name
of our horse?"

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:09.181
He goes, "It's Poco Bueno."

00:04:09.181 --> 00:04:10.616
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.616 --> 00:04:13.386
-I go, "Poco Bueno?"
I go, "What does that mean?"

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:16.622
He goes, "It means
a little bit good."

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:20.126
-Little bit good.
-I go, "Who --

00:04:20.126 --> 00:04:21.660
Why didn't we get Mucho Bueno?

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:25.430
I mean, I would have been happy
with Bueno,

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:26.966
regular Bueno."

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.300
I got Poco Bueno.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:32.304
And I went to OTB
to see his debut,

00:04:32.304 --> 00:04:34.740
and I put some money on him
with my friend.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:38.911
And he came in last place,
and I haven't seen him since.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.613
-Did you put him
in a claiming race,

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.448
or was it -- Did it get claimed?

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:45.385
-Yeah. It was in
a real, actual race.

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:48.154
It was in the gate. I know that.

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:50.322
-See, you just picture
like winning things

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:52.792
and in the circle and crying
and dreams coming true.

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:55.360
But the reality is,
someone's got to feed the horse,

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:57.796
and the horse has to be washed,
and there's a lot of expenses

00:04:57.796 --> 00:05:02.635
before Little Good -- Little Bit
Good gets a chance to race.

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:05.004
Little Bit Good
needs lots of food.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.372
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:09.274
What I heard, right now,
he's an Uber driver.

00:05:09.274 --> 00:05:11.511
And that's what I heard.
That's what he does now.

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:14.113
-But he's happy, Jimmy.
He's happy. He's happy.

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:15.548
-Yeah, he doesn't
like racing anymore.

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:17.649
It's not his thing, you know?

00:05:17.649 --> 00:05:20.219
You have a movie coming out,
"North Hollywood."

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:21.587
-Yes.

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:24.156
-This is -- Who -- Mikey Alfred.

00:05:24.156 --> 00:05:25.558
-Mikey Alfred.
Yeah, I did this movie.

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.693
I like this young filmmaker.
He's a young kid,

00:05:27.693 --> 00:05:29.495
and he comes from
the skateboard culture,

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.864
and he had like
a coming of age movie,

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:34.133
and I was just
really impressed with him.

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:35.835
So I said
that I would do the movie.

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.103
So, I'm glad that I did it.

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:38.571
It's a nice, little movie
that he made.

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:39.972
He's a first-time director.

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:43.242
And it's, like, this whole
skateboarding culture

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:44.276
that was very interesting.

00:05:44.276 --> 00:05:46.178
-Is it about his life?

00:05:46.178 --> 00:05:48.280
-It is. It's sort of
based on his life, yes.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:51.917
It's sort of based on his, kind
of, growing up skateboarding

00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:54.520
and making a decision
to pursue that.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.956
-Vince, I wanted to ask you --

00:05:56.956 --> 00:06:01.160
You act in a lot of movies.
You produce movies.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:04.596
And I was wondering
if you would play a game with me

00:06:04.596 --> 00:06:06.832
that is about --
-Yes, I'll play a game

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:10.168
as long as it doesn't involve
investing in horses

00:06:10.168 --> 00:06:11.604
or things of that nature.

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:13.639
-We'll talk about that
over the commercial break.

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:14.807
We'll discuss.
-Okay.

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:16.042
-Alright. Good.
More with Vince Vaughn.

